+# Agent Note: Win32 picker memory and IPC lifetime
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-27-win32-picker-electron-memory.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Selecting a folder under Electron 42.10.1 exits the dialog worker with code 134 at `readUtf16`. Koffi's `view` exposes native memory as an external ArrayBuffer, which Electron forbids. Opening or cancelling a dialog does not exercise that read. The worker also disconnects IPC after its `showing` notice, before the terminal message is guaranteed to flush.
+
+## Decision
+
+The [bindings](../../../../packages/host/directory-picker-native/src/win32-dialog-bindings.ts) copy NUL-terminated UTF-16 characters through `koffi.decode(address, 'char16', -1)` and free the COM string in `finally`. The worker disconnects only after `done` or `error` has flushed. Unexpected child exits report the code and signal.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**External memory views** cannot support Electron's memory cage. Checking only the low byte of each UTF-16 code unit also truncates valid directory names.
+
+**Decoding as `str16`** treats the raw character address as a pointer slot and adds an invalid dereference.
+
+**Changing the desktop framework** is unnecessary for a local path-decoding defect and would add backend packaging work.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The copy is proportional to one path string and preserves the existing native dialog and IPC protocol. Unit tests reject external buffers and exercise send-completion ordering. The desktop consumer owns an Electron artifact test with real Koffi decoding and mocked modal COM calls; real user selection remains a separate acceptance check.
